<runspec version="MOVES5.0.1">
	<description><![CDATA[Rates-scale (MESOSCALE_LOOKUP) twin of userdb-lev: DEFAULT domain, Washtenaw, 2020, August weekday hour 7, with a
USER INPUT DATABASE (<databaseselection> washtenaw_cdb) built EXACTLY as MOVES 5's
LEV tool builds it (county-inputs/washtenaw-userdb-lev/setup-lev.sql: the
MOVES5_MyLEVS_Template.sql of database/LEV_NLEVScripts/, keeping model-year groups
1999-2003 and 2010-2017): one table, emissionRateByAge, holding emissionRateByAgeLEV's
rows at those groups. MOVES merges user databases before the default database
(INSERT IGNORE), so those rows replace the default rates at their keys. Gasoline
passenger cars, passenger trucks and light commercial trucks (MOVES adds every
other fuel); THC, CO, NOx, NMHC and the PM2.5 group at running and start exhaust;
road types 1 and 5. The 1990-2020 cohorts read LEV rates at 1999-2003 and 2010-2017
and default rates at 1990-1998, 2004-2009 and 2018-2020. Captured for moves.esm
PLAN.md section 7.3.82 (LEV): the rate tables are written from BaseRateOutput, which reads the same merged emissionRateByAge. <scaleinputdatabase> is deliberately left empty with a
non-placeholder description, so the capture does not also name the user database as
a domain database.]]></description>
